      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-02T06:21:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess it\u0027s fine because spec *result points to the underlying entry in *rec. It\u0027s equivalent to:\n  int a \u003d 10;\n  int b \u003d 11;\n\n  int **p_array \u003d calloc(5, sizeof(int*));\n  p_array[0] \u003d \u0026a;\n  p_array[1] \u003d \u0026b;\n\n  int *p0 \u003d p_array[0]; \n  printf(\"%p, %p, %p\\n\", p_array[0], p_array[1], p0);\n  free(p_array);\n  printf(\"%p, %p\\n\", p0, p_array[0]);\n\n----\u003e\n0x7ffef20ced6c, 0x7ffef20ced68, 0x7ffef20ced6c\n0x7ffef20ced6c, (nil)",
